  "text_md": "Midwifery xxx (xxxx) xxx–xxx\n\nContents lists available at ScienceDirect\n\n# Midwifery\n\njournal homepage: www.elsevier.com/locate/midw\n\nCorrigendum\n\n# Corrigendum to “Midwifery continuity of carer in an area of high socio-\n\neconomic disadvantage in London: A retrospective analysis of Albany Midwifery Practice outcomes using routine data (1997–2009)” [Midwifery\n\n# 48 (2017) 1–10]\n\na,⁎ Caroline S.E. Homer, RM, MMed(ClinEpi), PhD Professor, Nicky Leap, DMid Adjunct Professor of Midwifery a, Nadine Edwards, PhD Independent Researcher a,b,c, Jane Sandall, PhD, CBE Professor, NIHR Senior Investigator b,c a Centre for Midwifery, Child and Family Health, Faculty of Health, University of Technology Sydney, PO Box 123, Broadway, Sydney, New South Wales 2007, Australia b Division of Women's Health, Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine, King's College London, United Kingdom c Women's Health Academic Centre, St. Thomas' Hospital, London SE1 7EH, United Kingdom\n\nThe authors regret that on page 8 we inadvertently referred to NICE as providing policy and policy direction. This was incorrect. NICE provides national clinical guidance based on systematic reviews. The sentence should read: A large study comparing perinatal outcomes by planned place of birth (Birthplace in England Collaborative Group, 2011) supported the clinical guidance to offer women with low risk pregnancies a choice of birth settings, including birth at home (NICE, 2014). The authors would like to apologise for any inconvenience caused.\n\nDOI of original article: [http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.02.009](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.02.009) ⁎ Corresponding author. E-mail address: caroline.homer@uts.edu.au (C.S.E. Homer). [http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013)\n\n0266-6138/ © 2017 The Author(s). Published by Elsevier Ltd. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license ([http://creativecommons.org/licenses/BY-NC-ND/4.0/](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/BY-NC-ND/4.0/)).\n\nPlease cite this article as: Homer, C., Midwifery (2017), [http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013)\n",
